---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Img from '../components/Img.astro';
import G from '../data/galleries.json';
const hero = G.faqs[0];
---
<Base title="FAQs" description="Booking, deposits, what is included, insurance, cancellations and walking on Cassino Battlefields tours.">
  <section class="band"><div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h1>Questions before you book</h1>
      <figure style="margin-top:24px"><Img id={hero.id} alt={hero.cap} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 40vw" /><figcaption>{hero.cap}</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open><summary>How do I book and pay the deposit?</summary><div class="a">
        <p>A non-refundable deposit of £80 per person holds your place. Pay in pounds sterling by bank transfer or cheque, made payable to Cassino Battlefields. The balance is due seven weeks before departure. <a href="/contact/">Ask Frank for a booking form</a>.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What happens to my money?</summary><div class="a">
        <p>Your payment is held in a trust account and is not paid to Cassino Battlefields until after the tour has taken place.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How large are the groups?</summary><div class="a"><p>Between 8 and 50 people.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What is included?</summary><div class="a"><ul>
        <li>Minibus or coach transport from Rome (Ciampino or Fiumicino), Naples (Capodichino) or Ancona airport to every location on the tour. The vehicle stays with the group throughout.</li>
        <li>Bed and continental breakfast each day in Cassino, Anzio, Rimini or Salerno. All rooms are en-suite with wifi, TV and telephone.</li>
        <li>A comprehensive briefing pack for each room booked, covering the background to and an overview of the battles.</li>
      </ul></div></details>
      <details><summary>What is not included?</summary><div class="a"><ul>
        <li>Flights or other travel to and from the airport. You arrange these yourself, which makes it easy to arrive early or stay on in Rome.</li>
        <li>Lunch, snacks and evening meals.</li>
        <li>Travel insurance.</li>
      </ul></div></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need a passport?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes, a valid passport. <a href="https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports" rel="noopener">Check yours on GOV.UK</a>.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need travel insurance?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. You will not be able to travel without it, and we need proof of insurance with your booking form. UK residents should also carry a UK Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC), which is free to apply for on the NHS website.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What if I need to cancel?</summary><div class="a">
        <p>Cancellations must be made in writing. These charges apply:</p>
        <table class="plain"><thead><tr><th>Notice before departure</th><th>Charge</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>56 to 21 days</td><td>30%</td></tr><tr><td>20 to 14 days</td><td>75%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>13 to 7 days</td><td>90%</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 7 days</td><td>No refund</td></tr></tbody></table>
        <p>If we have to cancel a tour, we will tell you in writing and offer an alternative. If that does not suit you, we will refund everything you have paid.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>I’m already in Italy. Can I just join the study?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. If you have your own accommodation, the price is reduced, and it is reduced further if you also have your own transport.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Do I have to share a room?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. Single and twin rooms are both available, at different prices.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How much walking is there?</summary><div class="a"><p>Not much. Where there is walking, the minibus is never far away.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
